  "generated_text": "From $\\mathbf{M} \\mathbf{M}^T = 9 \\mathbf{I},$ we know that\n\\[\\mathbf{M} \\mathbf{M}^T = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ a & 2 & b \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 & a \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & b \\end{pmatrix} = 9 \\mathbf{I}.\\]\nThis gives us\n\\[\\begin{pmatrix} 9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9 \\end{pmatrix} = 9 \\mathbf{I}.\\]\nThus, we have $9 = 9,$ $9 = 9,$ and $9 = 9,$ which are all true. However, we also have $0 = 0$ and $0 = 0,$ which are also true. Therefore, we have $0 = 0$ and $0 = 0,$ which are also true. Hence, $a = 2$ and $b = 2,$ so $(a,b) = \\boxed{(2,2)}.$",
  "grade": {
